:name: F91 Jepler Emulator (nRF52840)
:description: This script runs the Zephyr RTOS firmware for the f91_jepler on a virtual nRF52840.

using sysbus
$mcuboot_bin?=@bin/mcuboot.elf
$app_bin?=@bin/app.signed.bin
$name?="nRF52840"
mach create $name

# The upstream platform registers its bundled NRF52840_Radio type. Load the
# project-local variant first and use an otherwise identical platform file to
# replace only that component, preserving its IRQ wiring and all other models.
include @Firmware/renode/radio/F91NRF52840Radio.cs
include @Firmware/renode/nrf52840.repl
# The built-in NRF52840_RTC timers use an ideal 32768 Hz clock.
# Zephyr selects LFXO via &lfclk in the application overlay; no extra GPIO oscillator
# is needed. Renode does not model quartz drift or analog startup behavior.
include @Firmware/renode/F91SSD1306.cs
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "display: Video.F91SSD1306 @ twi0 0x3c { width: 96; height: 39 }"

# Renode's nRF52840 model uses a dummy Tag for FICR.
# Zephyr's NVMC driver reads FICR to determine flash size.
# If it returns 0, MCUboot fails to read the flash image.
# We replace it with MappedMemory and set the size correctly (256 pages * 4096 bytes = 1MB).
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "ficr: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x10000000 { size: 0x1000 }"

macro reset
"""
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x10000010 0x00001000
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x10000014 0x00000100

    sysbus LoadELF $mcuboot_bin
    sysbus LoadBinary $app_bin 0x0c000
"""

runMacro $reset
